# @desktop — minimal KDE Plasma 6 Wayland (plan/03, plan/09). Printing/CJK entries are
# filtered out by stage 30 when INCLUDE_PRINTING/INCLUDE_CJK_FONTS are 0 (marker comments
# below).
#
# This is a 1:1 functional mirror of the GNOME set it replaces, not a full Plasma install:
# session + compositor + settings + file manager + terminal + software centre, and nothing
# else. Applications are Flatpaks (plan/03), so there is no Ark, no Kate, no Okular and no
# Gwenview here for exactly the reasons file-roller and gnome-text-editor were dropped from
# the GNOME set: each is a preinstalled Flatpak (`FLATPAK_PREINSTALL` in build.conf), and each
# would cost a native dependency tail on a read-only root to save a Flatpak download. Spectacle
# and KDE Partition Manager (below, near dolphin/konsole) are the two exceptions, because for
# them it isn't a choice: neither has ever been published to Flathub.
kde-plasma/plasma-desktop
kde-plasma/plasma-workspace
kde-plasma/kwin
kde-plasma/systemsettings
kde-plasma/plasma-systemmonitor
kde-plasma/plasma-nm
kde-plasma/plasma-pa
kde-plasma/powerdevil
kde-plasma/bluedevil
kde-plasma/kscreen
kde-plasma/polkit-kde-agent
kde-plasma/kwallet-pam
kde-plasma/discover
kde-plasma/xdg-desktop-portal-kde
kde-plasma/breeze
# The GTK theming bridge, kept so Flatpak apps (Firefox is preinstalled) do not render as an
# unstyled GTK island. It is also the reason "remove all GNOME" cannot be literal: gtk
# hard-RDEPENDs adwaita-icon-theme, which RDEPENDs gnome-base/librsvg. See plan/09 §4 for the
# full enumerated residue — dropping these two packages removes almost all of it.
kde-plasma/breeze-gtk
kde-plasma/kde-gtk-config
kde-plasma/plasma-workspace-wallpapers
kde-plasma/plasma-login-manager  # the display manager; its System Settings KCM is built in
# /usr/share/wayland-sessions/plasma.desktop lives HERE, not in the display manager and not in
# plasma-workspace. It is a PDEPEND of plasma-workspace so it would arrive anyway, but its
# wayland/X flags are the real lever deciding whether an Xorg session exists at all
# (X? pulls kde-plasma/kwin-x11), so it is named explicitly.
kde-plasma/plasma-login-sessions
kde-frameworks/breeze-icons
kde-apps/dolphin
kde-apps/konsole
# Native because Flathub has no Spectacle: flathub/org.kde.spectacle carries only an unmerged
# "beta" branch (5 open PRs, 1 open issue, never released) — no `org.kde.Spectacle` or
# `org.kde.spectacle` app has ever shipped. kde-plasma/, not kde-apps/: the ebuild moved
# category upstream. Pulls one dependency not already in the image: media-libs/opencv
# (unconditional RDEPEND, used for the region auto-detect on capture). Everything else it
# needs — kpipewire, layer-shell-qt, prison, the xcb libs — is already pulled in by
# plasma-workspace/kwin's own screencast support. Pinned tree has 6.6.6 stable; 6.6.6-r1 and
# 6.7.4-r1 are both ~amd64 only, so no keyword exception is taken here.
kde-plasma/spectacle
# Native for the same reason as Spectacle above: no `org.kde.partitionmanager` (or any casing)
# has ever shipped on Flathub — plausibly because a disk partitioner is a bad sandbox fit in
# the first place. sys-block/, not kde-apps/ or kde-plasma/. IUSE is empty; the only dependency
# not already in the image is sys-libs/kpmcore, the backend library — no libparted pulled in,
# it drives sys-apps/util-linux (already in @base) directly. Privilege escalation goes through
# sys-auth/polkit-qt, already here for Discover/systemsettings.
sys-block/partitionmanager
kde-apps/kio-extras              # the gvfs equivalent: trash, network, thumbnails
kde-plasma/print-manager         #printing
sys-power/power-profiles-daemon
media-video/pipewire
media-video/wireplumber
x11-base/xwayland
media-fonts/noto
media-fonts/noto-emoji
media-fonts/noto-cjk             #cjk
net-print/cups                   #printing
